      "writtenOn": "2025-04-14T18:17:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On Graphite, this wasn\u0027t ever working because it only knew how to handle mask filters that used AutoLayer. On Ganesh, it had dedicated code to handle blurs and mask filters that could be converted to `GrFragmentProcessors`, and if that didn\u0027t work I believe it would run the mask filter on the CPU and then upload the texture. In that case, it would only work for certain types of SkMask data and I don\u0027t think 3D was one of them.  The goal will be for raster, Ganesh, and Graphite to all use AutoLayer.  I believe there is evidence that clients relying on the deprecated emboss filter have also forced their rendering to be on the raster backend to get the output they wanted.  When this is all done, it could mean they could go back to GPU rendering.\n\nI am not surprised that there is a mismatch between how the emboss lighting parameters are input vs. what the specular/diffuse parameters are expecting, but I will look to see if the heuristics make sense. I don\u0027t think we need to have it be exactly right as long the as approximate visual effect is preserved.\n\nCan we expand the emboss example to have some regular text and path draws?",
      "parentUuid": "0f33a41c_fc87a7e6",
      "revId": "1f6eda28bb16b54e59746c5a0881ebb49ca0a489",
