      "writtenOn": "2025-04-15T18:42:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The SkEmbossMaskFilter logic was implementing \"Phong\" specular lighting, whereas the SkLightingImageFilter logic is implementing \"Blinn-Phong\" specular lighting.\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blinn%E2%80%93Phong_reflection_model recommends multiplying by 4 to convert from a Phong specular exponent to a Blinn exponent.  In addition, though, SkEmbossMaskFilter documents `fLight.fSpecular` as being in fixed 4.4 format.\n\nTo convert to a scalar, we should divide by 16.f, which will preserve the lower four bits as fractional (whereas `\u003e\u003e 4` discards them). Combining that with the Blinn-Phong adjustment should mean we just have to pass in `fLight.fSpecular / 4.f` (no +1 anymore either)",
      "range": {
